   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Number of knowledge products made available to policy makers and the broader public that include gender analysis as a cross-cutting issue
2. Number of institutions engaged (through dialogue events, including stakeholders such as civil society, opinion leaders and government officials among others) to foster dialogue on the Report&apos;s theme
3. Number of downloads and single pageviews of AHDR materials and related pages</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2018">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. 6 (AHDRs between 2002 and 2016)
2. 0 (2014)
3. 4,428</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. 1 (Publication of the AHDR 2021 edition)
2. At least 30 institutions engaged (through dialogue events, including stakeholders such as civil society, opinion leaders and government officials among others) to foster dialogue on the AHDR 2021 research theme
3. At least 5,000 downloads and single pageviews of AHDR materials and related pages</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. 0 (Publication of AHDR 2021 postponed to 2022; 3 AHDR Background Research Papers: a. The Impact of COVID-19 on progress towards achieving the SDGs: using a human development lens to analyse the case of the Arab region; b. Assessing Multi-Sectoral Collaborations in the COVID-19 Pandemic Response in Selected Arab Countries; c. COVID-19 and Gender in the Arab States: Using a Human Development Lens to Explore the Gendered Risks, Outcomes and Impacts of the Pandemic on Women&#x2019;s Health; 2 AHDR Research Papers translated into Arabic)
2. 20 (*6 on paper a., 3 on paper b., 2 on paper c., 2 on a working paper titled Overlapping Fragilities: The Impact of COVID-19 on Refugees and IDPs in Conflict-Affected Countries in the MENA, 2 external reviewers for the AHDR draft, 3 AHDR Advisory Board members, 2 AHDR team
3. 17,095 unique page views on the AHDR website</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. 1 (AHDR 2022 edition)
2. At least 20 institutions (engaged through dialogue events, including stakeholders such as civil society, opinion leaders and government officials among others) to foster dialogue on the AHDR 2022 theme
3. At least 5,000 downloads and single pageviews of the AHDR 2022</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. 1 (AHDR 2022 edition titled Expanding opportunities for an Inclusive and Resilient Recovery in the Post-Covid Era in English and Arabic, and Executive Summary in English, Arabic and French)
2. 21(*7 at the global launch, 4 at the Washington DC event, 6 at the Beirut event, 3 external reviewers for the AHDR draft, 1 environment expert at the AUB)
3. 12,712 (*4,976 views of the English report across the UNDP and AHDR websites, 7,736 views of the Arabic report across both websites)</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. 1(Publication of AHDR 2020 edition)
2. At least 30 experts and academic institutions engaged to foster dialogue on the AHDR 2020 research theme
3. At least 5,000 downloads and single pageviews of AHDR 2020</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">In lieu of publishing a traditional full-fledged AHDR, this output pivoted to a more agile strategy given the incertitude created by COVID-19, which favoured shorter papers around thematic research as well as other by-products such as blogs, etc. All products delivered in 2020 will be used to position UNDP in relevant international, regional and national events, providing evidence and analysis to affirm UNDP&#x2019;s thought leadership in the region.
1.	0 (2 AHDR Research papers plus a dashboard; 3 blog posts: a.	Inclusive Citizenship and the Data Imperative in Arab Countries; b.	Citizenship 360&#xb0; in the Arab Region: Perceptions on Sustainable Development across Countries, Income and Gender; c.	Citizenship 360&#xb0;: Survey Dashboard; d.	Human vulnerability in Arab countries at the time of a pandemic; e.	Grappling with a crisis like no other: the fragility of Arab countries in the face of COVID-19; f.	On Brookings Website, Governance in the Arab region: Experts discuss public responses to COVID-19.)
2.  186 (*AHDR Webinar Series 2020: Human Development in the Arab States in the time of COVID-19. Participation in the first webinar reached 60 people, the second webinar 76 people. * A third webinar co-organized with the Atlantic Council involved 50 participants on the Zoom call, but reached 1,700 views on social media.)
3. 10,253 unique page views on the AHDR website</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
